A||||1||fotoman1||2.8L celebrity block
Z||000000||fotoman1||08-27-99||07:42 PM||||I just aquired a 1985 Fiero w/ a V6 in it. The car ran when I picked it up but shortly there after It threw a rod through the block. I was told that a 2.8L block from a celebrity will work. I plan on doing a full rebuild but it seams rather hard to find a used block from a Fiero. Any help would be appreciated.
Z||000001||terryk||08-27-99||10:18 PM||||Yes, a 2.8L Celebrity block will work. it has the larger crank journals you are looking for. 1985 Citation X-11 too. <p>Look for an 8th digit of W in the VIN of the Celebrity/Ciera.<p>The 3.1L blocks will work also. <p>I am assuming you will be using the 2.8L crank. If you swap to the 3.1L crank, the pistons will need to be for the iron head engine and you will need to change to the 88 or later flywheel/flexplate (needs to be neutral balanced).<p> 
